  "note": "Wiktionary's `phonemic_IPA` algorithm mixes phonemic and phonetic rules (cluster devoicing, schwa epenthesis, aspiration stripping in Western). Our v3 profiles implement strict Tier 1 phonemic transcription per Dum-Tragut 2009 and JIPA 2024. Cases marked `divergence_reason` are deliberate, documented divergences from Wiktionary; they are NOT regressions.",
  "divergence_categories": {
    "regressive_devoicing": "Tier 2 morphophonological rule (ղ → χ, վ → f before voiceless). Dum-Tragut 2009: 22 explicitly states these rules are not strict and general. Excluded from phonemic profile.",
    "lexical_devoicing": "Lexically restricted to a closed word list (հարավ, ավտո, նավթ per Dum-Tragut 2009: 30). Not a productive rule. Excluded.",
    "suffix_palatalization": "The -ությ- → -ut͡sʰj rule (Wiktionary-only). Dum-Tragut 2009: 35 explicitly transcribes the suffix as [utʰjun]. Excluded.",
    "western_aspiration_strip": "Wiktionary's broad phonemic strips Western aspiration on թ ք փ ց չ. JIPA 2024: 447-448 and Dolatian 2022 confirm Standard Western RETAINS aspiration. We retain it.",
    "western_progressive_devoicing": "Beirut-specific morphophonological rule (JIPA 2024: 458-459). Applies in derived environments only, not as a blind phonotactic rule. Excluded.",
    "schwa_epenthesis": "Tier 2 phonetic-level epenthesis (Dum-Tragut 2009: 30-35). Excluded.",
    "yu_to_y_glide": "Western յու → ʏ post-consonant. Documented as variable per Dolatian 2022 and JIPA 2024: 461. Not implemented; documented gap.",
    "ia_to_ja_glide": "Wiktionary's իա → /jɑ/ glide formation. Phonetic-level, not in primary sources as a phonemic rule."
  },
